Package: libvmod-cachetag
Architecture: any
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
 vinyld-abi-@VINYL_STRICT_ABI@,
 vinyld-vrt (= @VINYL_VRT@),
 vinyld-cohort-@COHORT_ID@,
Description: tag-based cache invalidation VMOD for Vinyl Cache
 cachetag is a Vinyl Cache VMOD that tags cached objects and invalidates them
 by tag. It maintains a purge map so a single tag purge can invalidate every
 object that carries the tag, without a full cache ban or a linear ban-list
 evaluation.
 .
 This package installs only the VMOD shared object, its manual page and its
 VCC interface description. It does not install a daemon, a service unit, a
 system user or any VCL, and it does not restart Vinyl Cache.
 .
 The module declares "$ABI strict" and uses private Vinyl Cache cache APIs,
 so a given binary works only with the exact Vinyl Cache build it was
 compiled against. That coupling is encoded as a dependency on two virtual
 packages
 .
   vinyld-abi-@VINYL_STRICT_ABI@
   vinyld-cohort-@COHORT_ID@
 .
 which only the matching Vinyl Cache runtime provides, so an incompatible
 Vinyl Cache upgrade is unresolvable rather than silently loadable.
 .
 The two are not redundant. The ABI token is derived from the upstream Vinyl
 Cache source revision, so a repackaged, patched or vendor-respun runtime built
 from the same revision advertises the identical token and would otherwise
 satisfy this dependency without ever having been built or tested with this
 VMOD. The cohort id identifies the coordinated set of packages -- one Vinyl
 Cache runtime and every strict-ABI VMOD -- that were built and tested
 together, so a same-ABI runtime from a different cohort is refused.
